I put limited two-weaponing into my teensy-little ZAngband variant.

http://www.geocities.com/arthur_odwyer/myband/2hand.txt

Basically, you have 'two-handed', 'one-handed', and 'half-handed' weapons
(e.g., quarterstaves, longswords, and daggers, respectively).  You can't
wield a shield with a two-handed weapon.  You can't wield two one-handed
weapons at once.  You can't wield another weapon with a two-handed weapon.
You can't wear a bow in addition to two weapons (Angband has a separate
bow slot).  Two weapons get 1.75 as many attacks as one weapon, rounded
down [which would probably not apply as well to Nethack].

The real tricky part would be looking up all those weapons in the
dictionary, to find out whether a 'main gauche' is bigger or smaller
than a 'bec de corbin.' ;-)

And if you're *really* going for two-weapon realism, you'd disallow
wielding, say, a rapier and a long sword together -- that kind of
fighting would be like rubbing your stomach and patting your head
at the same time!

That's all.
